From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: DockSeed <dockseed@proton.me>
Date: Fri, 2 Oct 2026 02:00:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] clk: sunxi-ng: a733: the audio PLLs, I2S/OWA/DMIC module clocks, bus gates and resets

Nothing on the audio side of the A733 is in our CCU: neither audio PLL,
none of the I2S/PCM0-4, OWA (S/PDIF) and DMIC module clocks, gates or
resets. This adds 21 clocks and 7 resets.

The register map, field by field, is in the block comment
in front of the new clocks. The decisions:

- PLL_AUDIO0 (0x0260) is integer-N plus one fractional point, the UM's
  own: Table 4-3, N 67 + FRAC 0x179A7, VCO 1625.7024 MHz, which P0 = 18
  turns into 90.3168 MHz = 22.5792 MHz x 4, the 44.1 kHz family exact.
  It is programmed as UM 4.1.3.5 "fractional division" (SIG_DELT_PAT_EN
  1, FRAC_EN 0, WAVE_STEP 0, WAVE_BOT = fraction x 2^17) through
  ccu_sdm, which writes the pattern before it sets the master switch:
  the order of 4.1.4.1 steps 2-4. PLL_PI_EN (PAT1 bit 31) is set at
  probe, as step 2 recommends; the other static parameters stay at their
  defaults. A first draft modelled no fractional point at all and left
  44.1 kHz approximate; the UM V1.00 procedure is enough to do it right.
  The sdm pattern carries SIG_DELT_PAT_EN (bit 31), as every mainline
  table does, because ccu_sdm_helper_read_rate() compares the pattern with
  the whole PAT0 register; the static half is written at probe so the
  helper's write only adds the master switch. On a first cut without bit 31
  (the 8 GiB board, 2026-10-02) the PLL locked at the right point (CTRL 0xF97F4200,
  PAT0 0xE00179A7) but recalc reported 0 Hz and the 4X tap divided by 128.
- PLL_AUDIO1 (0x0280) has two taps, DIV2 (P0) and DIV5 (P1), and one
  output gate (bit 27). The gate is part of the PLL's enable mask so
  neither tap can close it under the other. Its defaults are the UM's
  48 kHz point (DIV5 = 614.4 MHz, /25 = 24.576 MHz exactly), and its taps
  do not propagate rate requests: two blocks on two taps would retune
  each other.
- Both PLLs get LDO_EN and LOCK_ENABLE at probe, PLL_EN stays the
  clock's own enable -- the treatment the video and VE PLLs get.
- OWA_RX has only mux value 010 (PERI0_400M) documented; 000 and 001 are
  Reserved, so it is a one-entry mux table. The vendor lists 200M, 300M
  and 400M at 0, 1, 2; that does not match the UM and is not carried.
- Bus gates take ahb by this driver's convention; the UM names no parent.

Rejected from the A523 and the vendor: the A523's PLL_AUDIO0 sits at
0x078 with its enable at bit 27 (here 0x0260, bit 31); its 22.5792 MHz
point (N 75, M 20, pattern 0xc000872b) and the vendor's copy of it
(0xA002872B) are not the UM's; its 98.304 MHz point at N 49 puts the VCO
at 1.18 GHz, under this PLL's 1.26 GHz floor (Table 4-2).

Silicon, the 8 GiB board, our 6.18.54 kernel, 2026-10-02: PLL_AUDIO0_CTRL =
0x41145500, PLL_AUDIO1_CTRL = 0x41147F00 (off, N/P at the documented
defaults), every I2S/OWA/DMIC clock and gate register 0, AUDIOPLL_GATE_EN
= 0x00070007. Bit 24 reads 1 in both PLL registers although the UM marks
[26:23] reserved; all writes are read-modify-write and keep it.

Ids: clocks 115-135, resets 41-47.

Verified: applies, builds. Silicon effect is owed to the consumers.

Assisted-by: Claude
---
--- a/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60iw2.c
+++ b/drivers/clk/sunxi-ng/ccu-sun60iw2.c
@@ -2218,6 +2218,213 @@ static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_dma1_clk,  "bus-dma1",  ahb_hws, 0x070C, BIT(0), 0
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(mbus_dma0_clk, "mbus-dma0", ahb_hws, 0x05E4, BIT(0), 0);
 static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(mbus_dma1_clk, "mbus-dma1", ahb_hws, 0x05E4, BIT(3), 0);
 
+/*
+ * Audio: the two audio PLLs, the module clocks and bus gates of I2S/PCM0-4,
+ * OWA (S/PDIF) and DMIC. UM V1.00 section 4.1 (CCU) and its register descriptions.
+ *
+ *   PLL_AUDIO0_CTRL 0x0260, reset 0x4014_5500
+ *     31 PLL_EN  30 LDO_EN  29 LOCK_ENABLE  28 LOCK (R)  27 PLL_OUTPUT_GATE
+ *     22:16 PLL_P0, P0 = field + 1 (7 bits)  15:8 PLL_N, N = field + 1,
+ *     PLL_N >= 11, so N >= 12  1 PLL_INPUT_DIV, M1
+ *     AUDIO0PLL4X = 24MHz * N / M1 / P0
+ *   PLL_AUDIO1_CTRL 0x0280, reset 0x4014_7F00
+ *     the same control bits, N and M1; 22:20 PLL_P0 and 18:16 PLL_P1, each
+ *     field + 1; AUDIO1PLL_DIV2 = 24MHz * N / M1 / P0, AUDIO1PLL_DIV5 =
+ *     24MHz * N / M1 / P1 -- default rates 1536 MHz and 614.4 MHz (24.576Mhz*25).
+ *     DIV2 and DIV5 name the default dividers, not
+ *     fixed ratios. One PLL_OUTPUT_GATE (27) serves both taps.
+ *   Table 4-2: AUDIO0 Fvco 1.26G~2.52G, P0 1~128; AUDIO1 Fvco 1.8G~3.1G,
+ *     P0/P1 1~8; reference 24MHz
+ *   Table 4-3: AUDIO0 N 67 + FRAC 0x179A7, VCO 1625.7024, 90.3168 =
+ *     22.5792 * 4; AUDIO1 N 128, VCO 3072, 1536/614.4, 24.576
+ *   AUDIOPLL_GATE_EN 0x191C, reset 0x0007_0007: bits 16-18 gate the 4X,
+ *     DIV2 and DIV5 taps, all open at reset
+ *
+ *   I2SPCMn_CLK 0x1200 + n * 0x10 (n = 0..4): 31 gate, 26:24 mux (000
+ *     AUDIO0PLL4X, 001 AUDIO1PLL_DIV2, 010 AUDIO1PLL_DIV5, 011 PERI0_200M),
+ *     4:0 M = field + 1
+ *   I2SPCM2_ASRC_CLK 0x1224: the same, mux adds 011 PERI0_300M,
+ *     100 PERI1_300M
+ *   I2SPCMn_BGR 0x120C + n * 0x10: 0 gating, 16 reset
+ *   OWA_TX_CLK 0x1280: 31 gate, mux 000 4X, 001 DIV2, 010 DIV5, 4:0 M
+ *
+ *   OWA_RX_CLK 0x1284: mux 000 and 001 Reserved, 010 PERI0_400M
+ *   OWA_BGR 0x128C, DMIC_CLK 0x12C0 (mux as OWA_TX), DMIC_BGR 0x12CC
+ *
+ *
+ * Silicon, the 8 GiB board, our 6.18.54 kernel, 2026-10-02: PLL_AUDIO0_CTRL = 0x41145500,
+ * PLL_AUDIO1_CTRL = 0x41147F00 (both PLLs off, N/P at their documented
+ * defaults), every I2S/OWA/DMIC clock and bus-gate register 0x00000000,
+ * AUDIOPLL_GATE_EN = 0x00070007. ⚠ Bit 24 reads 1 in both PLL registers
+ * although the UM marks [26:23] reserved with no default; every write here is
+ * read-modify-write, so it is kept as found.
+ *
+ * What this models, and what it leaves out:
+ * - PLL_AUDIO0 has one fractional point, the UM's own: Table 4-3's N 67 + FRAC
+ *   0x179A7, VCO 1625.7024 MHz, which P0 = 18 turns into 90.3168 MHz =
+ *   22.5792 MHz * 4 -- the 44.1 kHz family, exact. It is programmed as UM
+ *   4.1.3.5 "fractional division": SIG_DELT_PAT_EN 1, FRAC_EN 0,
+ *   WAVE_STEP 0, so WAVE_BOT (PAT0 [16:0]) carries the fraction x * 2^17.
+ *   ccu_sdm writes the pattern with the master switch clear and sets it after,
+ *   which is the order of 4.1.4.1 steps 2-4. Static parameters
+ *   per step 2: SPR_FREQ_MODE 3 in the pattern, PLL_PI_EN 1 (PAT1 bit 31) at
+ *   probe, PLL_PI_CFG, SMOOTH_EN and DITHER left at their defaults (3, 0, 0).
+ *   Every other PLL_AUDIO0 rate is integer-N.
+ * - PLL_AUDIO1 carries no CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT on its taps: its defaults are the
+ *   UM's own 48 kHz point (DIV5 / 25 = 24.576 MHz exactly), and two blocks on
+ *   two taps would otherwise retune each other's rate. PLL_AUDIO0's tap does
+ *   propagate, so a request for the 44.1 kHz family can move it.
+ * - PLL_AUDIO1's single output gate (27) is part of the PLL's enable mask, so
+ *   neither tap can switch it off under the other.
+ * - The bus gates take ahb_hws by this file's convention; the UM names no
+ *   parent for them ("see CCU"). Only the enable bit is consumed.
+ */
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_REG		0x0260
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO1_REG		0x0280
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO_LDO_EN	BIT(30)
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO_LOCK_ENABLE	BIT(29)
+
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT0_REG	0x0268
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT1_REG	0x026C
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_PAT0_SIG_DELT_PAT_EN	BIT(31)
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_PAT1_PI_EN		BIT(31)
+
+/*
+ * PAT0 for the Table 4-3 point: SIG_DELT_PAT_EN (31) = 1, SPR_FREQ_MODE
+ * [30:29] = 3, WAVE_STEP [28:20] = 0, SDM_DIRECTION 0, FREQ 0, WAVE_BOT [16:0]
+ * = 0x179A7 (0.73760 * 2^17). 24 MHz * (67 + 0x179A7 / 2^17) = 1625.70245 MHz;
+ * the table names the UM's 1625.7024 MHz, which P0 = 18 divides to 90.3168 MHz
+ * exactly.
+ *
+ * The pattern carries the enable bit because ccu_sdm_helper_read_rate()
+ * compares it with the whole register (ccu_sdm.c), as every mainline table
+ * does. A first cut left bit 31 out: the PLL ran at the right point
+ * (PLL_AUDIO0 0xF97F4200, PAT0 0xE00179A7, locked; the 8 GiB board, 2026-10-02) but
+ * recalc never matched, reported 0 Hz, and the 4X tap divided by 128. The UM's
+ * order -- static parameters before the master switch (4.1.4.1 steps 2-4) --
+ * is kept by writing the static half at probe (sun60iw2_ccu_probe()), so the
+ * helper's pattern write only adds bit 31.
+ */
+#define SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT0_STATIC	0x600179a7
+static struct ccu_sdm_setting pll_audio0_sdm_table[] = {
+	{ .rate = 1625702400, .pattern = 0xe00179a7, .m = 1, .n = 67 },
+};
+
+static struct ccu_nm pll_audio0_clk = {
+	.enable		= BIT(31),
+	.lock		= BIT(28),
+	.n		= _SUNXI_CCU_MULT_OFFSET_MIN_MAX(8, 8, 1, 12, 255),
+	.m		= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV(1, 1),
+	.sdm		= _SUNXI_CCU_SDM(pll_audio0_sdm_table, 0,
+					 SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT0_REG,
+					 SUN60IW2_PLL_PAT0_SIG_DELT_PAT_EN),
+	.min_rate	= 1260000000U,
+	.max_rate	= 2520000000U,
+	.common		= {
+		.reg		= SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_REG,
+		.features	= CCU_FEATURE_SIGMA_DELTA_MOD,
+		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT_PARENTS_HW("pll-audio0",
+				pll_ref_hws, &ccu_nm_ops,
+				CLK_SET_RATE_UNGATE),
+	},
+};
+static const struct clk_hw *pll_audio0_hws[] = { &pll_audio0_clk.common.hw };
+
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_HWS_WITH_GATE(audio0_pll4x_clk, "audio0-pll4x",
+				 pll_audio0_hws, SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_REG,
+				 16, 7, BIT(27), CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+
+static struct ccu_nm pll_audio1_clk = {
+	.enable		= BIT(31) | BIT(27),
+	.lock		= BIT(28),
+	.n		= _SUNXI_CCU_MULT_OFFSET_MIN_MAX(8, 8, 1, 12, 255),
+	.m		= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV(1, 1),
+	.min_rate	= 1800000000U,
+	.max_rate	= 3100000000U,
+	.common		= {
+		.reg		= SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO1_REG,
+		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT_PARENTS_HW("pll-audio1",
+				pll_ref_hws, &ccu_nm_ops,
+				CLK_SET_RATE_UNGATE),
+	},
+};
+static const struct clk_hw *pll_audio1_hws[] = { &pll_audio1_clk.common.hw };
+
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_HWS(audio1_pll_div2_clk, "audio1-pll-div2", pll_audio1_hws,
+		       SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO1_REG, 20, 3, 0);
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_HWS(audio1_pll_div5_clk, "audio1-pll-div5", pll_audio1_hws,
+		       SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO1_REG, 16, 3, 0);
+
+static const struct clk_parent_data i2s_parents[] = {
+	{ .hw = &audio0_pll4x_clk.common.hw },	/* 000 AUDIO0PLL4X    */
+	{ .hw = &audio1_pll_div2_clk.common.hw },/* 001 AUDIO1PLL_DIV2 */
+	{ .hw = &audio1_pll_div5_clk.common.hw },/* 010 AUDIO1PLL_DIV5 */
+	{ .hw = &pll_peri0_200m_clk.hw },	/* 011 PERI0_200M     */
+};
+
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(i2s0_clk, "i2s0", i2s_parents, 0x1200,
+				      0, 5, 24, 3, BIT(31), CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(i2s1_clk, "i2s1", i2s_parents, 0x1210,
+				      0, 5, 24, 3, BIT(31), CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(i2s2_clk, "i2s2", i2s_parents, 0x1220,
+				      0, 5, 24, 3, BIT(31), CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(i2s3_clk, "i2s3", i2s_parents, 0x1230,
+				      0, 5, 24, 3, BIT(31), CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(i2s4_clk, "i2s4", i2s_parents, 0x1240,
+				      0, 5, 24, 3, BIT(31), CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+
+static const struct clk_parent_data i2s2_asrc_parents[] = {
+	{ .hw = &audio0_pll4x_clk.common.hw },	/* 000 AUDIO0PLL4X    */
+	{ .hw = &audio1_pll_div2_clk.common.hw },/* 001 AUDIO1PLL_DIV2 */
+	{ .hw = &audio1_pll_div5_clk.common.hw },/* 010 AUDIO1PLL_DIV5 */
+	{ .hw = &pll_peri0_300m_clk.hw },	/* 011 PERI0_300M     */
+	{ .hw = &pll_peri1_300m_clk.hw },	/* 100 PERI1_300M     */
+};
+
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(i2s2_asrc_clk, "i2s2-asrc",
+				      i2s2_asrc_parents, 0x1224,
+				      0, 5, 24, 3, BIT(31), 0);
+
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_i2s0_clk, "bus-i2s0", ahb_hws, 0x120C, BIT(0), 0);
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_i2s1_clk, "bus-i2s1", ahb_hws, 0x121C, BIT(0), 0);
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_i2s2_clk, "bus-i2s2", ahb_hws, 0x122C, BIT(0), 0);
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_i2s3_clk, "bus-i2s3", ahb_hws, 0x123C, BIT(0), 0);
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_i2s4_clk, "bus-i2s4", ahb_hws, 0x124C, BIT(0), 0);
+
+static const struct clk_parent_data owa_dmic_parents[] = {
+	{ .hw = &audio0_pll4x_clk.common.hw },	/* 000 AUDIO0PLL4X    */
+	{ .hw = &audio1_pll_div2_clk.common.hw },/* 001 AUDIO1PLL_DIV2 */
+	{ .hw = &audio1_pll_div5_clk.common.hw },/* 010 AUDIO1PLL_DIV5 */
+};
+
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(owa_tx_clk, "owa-tx", owa_dmic_parents,
+				      0x1280, 0, 5, 24, 3, BIT(31),
+				      CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+
+/* OWA_RX: only mux value 010 is documented; 000 and 001 are Reserved. */
+static const struct clk_parent_data owa_rx_parents[] = {
+	{ .hw = &pll_peri0_400m_clk.hw },	/* 010 PERI0_400M     */
+};
+static const u8 owa_rx_table[] = { 2 };
+static struct ccu_div owa_rx_clk = {
+	.enable	= BIT(31),
+	.div	= _SUNXI_CCU_DIV(0, 5),
+	.mux	= _SUNXI_CCU_MUX_TABLE(24, 3, owa_rx_table),
+	.common	= {
+		.reg		= 0x1284,
+		.hw.init	= CLK_HW_INIT_PARENTS_DATA("owa-rx",
+							   owa_rx_parents,
+							   &ccu_div_ops, 0),
+	},
+};
+
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_owa_clk, "bus-owa", ahb_hws, 0x128C, BIT(0), 0);
+
+static SUNXI_CCU_M_DATA_WITH_MUX_GATE(dmic_clk, "dmic", owa_dmic_parents,
+				      0x12C0, 0, 5, 24, 3, BIT(31),
+				      CLK_SET_RATE_PARENT);
+static SUNXI_CCU_GATE_HWS(bus_dmic_clk, "bus-dmic", ahb_hws, 0x12CC, BIT(0), 0);
+
 /* ccu_common-based clocks (registered and reset-mapped by the core). */
 static struct ccu_common *sun60iw2_ccu_clks[] = {
 	&pll_ref_clk.common,
@@ -2322,6 +2529,27 @@ static struct ccu_common *sun60iw2_ccu_clks[] = {
 	&bus_dma1_clk.common,
 	&mbus_dma0_clk.common,
 	&mbus_dma1_clk.common,
+	&pll_audio0_clk.common,
+	&audio0_pll4x_clk.common,
+	&pll_audio1_clk.common,
+	&audio1_pll_div2_clk.common,
+	&audio1_pll_div5_clk.common,
+	&i2s0_clk.common,
+	&i2s1_clk.common,
+	&i2s2_clk.common,
+	&i2s3_clk.common,
+	&i2s4_clk.common,
+	&i2s2_asrc_clk.common,
+	&bus_i2s0_clk.common,
+	&bus_i2s1_clk.common,
+	&bus_i2s2_clk.common,
+	&bus_i2s3_clk.common,
+	&bus_i2s4_clk.common,
+	&owa_tx_clk.common,
+	&owa_rx_clk.common,
+	&bus_owa_clk.common,
+	&dmic_clk.common,
+	&bus_dmic_clk.common,
 };
 
 static struct clk_hw_onecell_data sun60iw2_hw_clks = {
@@ -2441,8 +2669,29 @@ static struct clk_hw_onecell_data sun60iw2_hw_clks = {
 		[CLK_BUS_DMA1]		= &bus_dma1_clk.common.hw,
 		[CLK_MBUS_DMA0]		= &mbus_dma0_clk.common.hw,
 		[CLK_MBUS_DMA1]		= &mbus_dma1_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_PLL_AUDIO0]	= &pll_audio0_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_AUDIO0PLL4X]	= &audio0_pll4x_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_PLL_AUDIO1]	= &pll_audio1_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_AUDIO1PLL_DIV2]	= &audio1_pll_div2_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_AUDIO1PLL_DIV5]	= &audio1_pll_div5_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_I2S0]		= &i2s0_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_I2S1]		= &i2s1_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_I2S2]		= &i2s2_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_I2S3]		= &i2s3_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_I2S4]		= &i2s4_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_I2S2_ASRC]		= &i2s2_asrc_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_BUS_I2S0]		= &bus_i2s0_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_BUS_I2S1]		= &bus_i2s1_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_BUS_I2S2]		= &bus_i2s2_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_BUS_I2S3]		= &bus_i2s3_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_BUS_I2S4]		= &bus_i2s4_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_OWA_TX]		= &owa_tx_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_OWA_RX]		= &owa_rx_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_BUS_OWA]		= &bus_owa_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_DMIC]		= &dmic_clk.common.hw,
+		[CLK_BUS_DMIC]		= &bus_dmic_clk.common.hw,
 	},
-	.num	= CLK_MBUS_DMA1 + 1,
+	.num	= CLK_BUS_DMIC + 1,
 };
 
 static struct ccu_reset_map sun60iw2_ccu_resets[] = {
@@ -2493,6 +2742,13 @@ static struct ccu_reset_map sun60iw2_ccu_resets[] = {
 	[RST_BUS_VE_DEC]	= { 0x0A8C, BIT(18) },
 	[RST_BUS_DMA0]		= { 0x0704, BIT(16) },
 	[RST_BUS_DMA1]		= { 0x070C, BIT(16) },
+	[RST_BUS_I2S0]		= { 0x120C, BIT(16) },
+	[RST_BUS_I2S1]		= { 0x121C, BIT(16) },
+	[RST_BUS_I2S2]		= { 0x122C, BIT(16) },
+	[RST_BUS_I2S3]		= { 0x123C, BIT(16) },
+	[RST_BUS_I2S4]		= { 0x124C, BIT(16) },
+	[RST_BUS_OWA]		= { 0x128C, BIT(16) },
+	[RST_BUS_DMIC]		= { 0x12CC, BIT(16) },
 };
 
 static const struct sunxi_ccu_desc sun60iw2_ccu_desc = {
@@ -2527,6 +2783,12 @@ static const u32 ve_pll_regs[] = {
 	SUN60IW2_PLL_VE1_REG,
 };
 
+/* The audio PLLs: the same -- LDO_EN and LOCK_ENABLE only. */
+static const u32 audio_pll_regs[] = {
+	SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_REG,
+	SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO1_REG,
+};
+
 static int sun60iw2_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 {
 	void __iomem *reg;
@@ -2636,6 +2898,38 @@ static int sun60iw2_ccu_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 		writel(val, reg + ve_pll_regs[i]);
 	}
 
+	/*
+	 * The audio PLLs, for the reason the video and VE PLLs above give: both
+	 * are off at reset with LOCK_ENABLE 0 (silicon, the 8 GiB board, 2026-10-02:
+	 * 0x41145500 and 0x41147F00), and LOCK only reports once LOCK_ENABLE is
+	 * set. PLL_EN stays the clock's own enable.
+	 */
+	for (i = 0; i < ARRAY_SIZE(audio_pll_regs); i++) {
+		val = readl(reg + audio_pll_regs[i]);
+		val |= SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO_LDO_EN | SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO_LOCK_ENABLE;
+		writel(val, reg + audio_pll_regs[i]);
+	}
+
+	/*
+	 * PLL_AUDIO0's fractional point needs phase interpolation on: a static
+	 * parameter, set once before SIG_DELT_PAT_EN can ever be set (UM
+	 * 4.1.4.1 step 2: PLL_PI_EN = 1 is recommended).
+	 */
+	val = readl(reg + SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT1_REG);
+	val |= SUN60IW2_PLL_PAT1_PI_EN;
+	writel(val, reg + SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT1_REG);
+
+	/*
+	 * And the fractional point's static half (SPR_FREQ_MODE, WAVE_BOT) in
+	 * PAT0 with the master switch still clear, unless the switch is already
+	 * on: then a boot stage has the PLL running fractionally and the write
+	 * is left to the clock framework.
+	 */
+	val = readl(reg + SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT0_REG);
+	if (!(val & SUN60IW2_PLL_PAT0_SIG_DELT_PAT_EN))
+		writel(SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT0_STATIC,
+		       reg + SUN60IW2_PLL_AUDIO0_PAT0_REG);
+
 	return devm_sunxi_ccu_probe(&pdev->dev, reg, &sun60iw2_ccu_desc);
 }
 
